 20061204
#
# This file contains ground state and inner shell non-relativistic
# photoionization cross sections for atoms and ions of elements up
# to Zn.
#
# The data in this file come from two papers:
#
# - Verner & Yakovlev 1995, A&AS, 109, 125
#   https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1995A%26AS..109..125V
#
#   This paper provides fits to both valence and inner shell ionization.
#   It makes up the first portion of the file, terminated by a line
#   with three '-1's.
#
# - Verner, Ferland, Korista, & Yakovlev 1996, ApJ, 465, 487
#   https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1996ApJ...465..487V
#
#   This paper provides fits to valence shell ionization only.
#   It makes up the second portion of the file.
#
# The data below accommodate the fitting formulae in these papers.
# The file begins with 3 lines of a data preamble is followed by
# these tables.
#
# In the 1995 paper, 7 shells in total are modeled, from 1s to 4s.
# Because the fitting formula depends on the orbital angular momentum
# of the shell, the first line of the data preamble lists their values
# (1s->0, 2s->0, 2p->1, etc). 
#
# The 1996 paper contains fits that extend from "the ionization
# threshold up to the first jump due to inner shell photoionization".
# This restriction is captured by the second line of data preamble --
# it holds the lower bound shell indices for the application of the
# 1996 formula, 30 values in total (one for each additional electron).
#
# The final line of data preamble contains 30 values for the shell
# indices that each additional electron would find itself in.
# Note that some 4th row elements start filling the 4s shell (index 7)
# before completing 3d (index 6); this is not captured below, but it is
# treated in the Cloudy source.
#
# The tables that make up the bulk of the file are derived from Table 1
# in each paper.
#
# Table 1 below:
# Col	Quantity	Units	Note
# ---	--------	----	----
# 1	nshell-1		shell index, in C scale
# 2	ne-1			number of electrons in ion, in C scale
# 3	Z-1			atomic number, in C scale
# 4	Eth		eV	threshhold energy; valence values outdated
# 5	E0		eV
# 6	sigma0		Mbarn	cross section normalization
# 7	y(a)
# 8	P
# 9	y(w)
#
# Columns 5-9 are the parameters employed in the fitting formula,
# eqn. (1) in 1995 paper. 
# See also online table:
# 	https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/viz-bin/cat/J/A+AS/109/125
#
#
# Table 2 below:
# Col	Quantity	Units	Note
# ---	--------	----	----
# 1	ne-1			number of electrons in ion, in C scale
# 2	Z-1			atomic number, in C scale
# 3	E0		eV
# 4	sigma0		Mbarn	cross section normalization
# 5	y(a)
# 6	P
# 7	y(w)
# 8	y0
# 9	y1
#
# Columns 3-9 are parameters employed in the fitting formula,
# eqn. (1) in 1996 paper; see Table 1 therein.
#
# THE NEW NUMBERS IN THIS FILE ARE INTRODUCED IN THE BRANCH STERLING
# TO FIT PHOTOIONIZATION OF EXTRA ELEMENTS, NEW INNER SHELLS AND EXTRA
# ELECTRONS' SHELLS UP TO Z=54. THESE DATA MUST BE CHECKED VALID.
